&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;sx&lt;/code&gt; prop lets you adjust spacing, colours, and layout inline, using your theme's values. The theme itself is customisable — change the primary colour, the font, or the border radius in one place and every component follows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MUI includes far more than forms: data grids with sorting and pagination, date pickers, autocomplete, drawers, snackbars, steppers, and charts. The components are accessible by default, with keyboard support and ARIA attributes built in, which saves a lot of work on admin panels and dashboards.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The tradeoff is bundle size and a distinctive look. MUI adds weight to your app, and out of the box every MUI app looks a bit like every other MUI app — though theming goes a long way. If you need a custom, brand-heavy design, a headless library may fit better.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MUI is for React developers building dashboards, admin panels, and internal tools who want a large set of solid, accessible components without designing each one from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
